What is derived, and how
========================

Every derived function body is in cold/memcold, and each takes from a single
upstream package, common/persistence/sql; the patch under patches/ is the
exception and is listed with them. The reason is the same throughout
cold/memcold: a folded window is written in one transaction spanning many
workflows, and the functions upstream writes a single workflow with are
unexported, so their statement sequences are copied rather than called.

Upstream error text is also reproduced in two files outside cold/memcold, and
they are listed below as well. No logic there is upstream's; the strings are,
and this notice treats a verbatim upstream error string as something to
disclose wherever it appears.

cold/memcold/rows.go
    Derived throughout, from execution_util.go (applyWorkflowMutationTx,
    applyWorkflowSnapshotTxAsReset, applyWorkflowSnapshotTxAsNew, applyTasks,
    createImmediateTasks, createScheduledTasks and the four per-table task
    inserts, buildExecutionRow, createExecution, updateExecution,
    lockExecution), from execution_state_map.go (its six update-and-delete
    pairs, one per keyed map) and execution_state_non_map.go
    (updateSignalsRequested, deleteSignalsRequestedSet, updateBufferedEvents,
    deleteBufferedEvents), from execution_tasks.go (the rangeComplete* family)
    and from execution.go (DeleteWorkflowExecution, getStartTimeFromState).
    The statement sequence of each write path is upstream's, and every row and
    filter literal — the executions row, the seven keyed tables, buffered events,
    the six task tables, the range-delete filters — is field-for-field
    identical. startTimeOf is getStartTimeFromState with its identifiers
    renamed. Error strings are this repository's own except one that is
    upstream's verbatim, in both places a task category is switched on:
    "unknown task category type: %v" (persistence_metric_clients.go). One
    function takes less than that: lockCurrent follows
    lockCurrentExecutionIfExists in shape and filter only, and issues a
    different statement.

cold/memcold/current.go
    GetCurrentExecutionWithLastWriteVersion and currentRowResponse are
    execution.go's GetCurrentExecution: the same select, the same response
    literal, and both of its error strings verbatim, "GetCurrentExecution
    operation failed. Error: %v" and the bare text of sql.ErrNoRows. What is
    added is the last_write_version column, which upstream's response type has
    nowhere to carry.

cold/memcold/apply.go
    One literal and its two statements: the sqlplugin.CurrentExecutionsRow that
    writeCurrentRow builds is field-for-field the one execution.go's
    createWorkflowExecutionTx builds, and the insert-or-update around it does
    what execution_util.go's createOrUpdateCurrentExecution and
    updateCurrentExecution do in their two writing modes — chosen here by
    whether the row was found rather than by a create mode. The rest of the
    file — the drain's transaction, its ordering, its assertions and its
    refusals — is not derived.

fold/check.go
    One error string, verbatim: "Encounter workflow db version mismatch,
    request db version: %v, actual db version: %v", from
    common/persistence/cassandra/errors.go. The layer refuses a run-row
    assertion in the store's own words so that a halted shard's log reads the
    same whichever of the two raised it. No logic here is upstream's.

cycle/read.go
    One error string, verbatim: "workflow execution not found for workflow ID
    %q and run ID %q", from common/persistence/execution_manager.go, for the
    same reason — a read served out of the window must be indistinguishable
    from the store's. No logic here is upstream's.

patches/temporal/0001-custom-persistence-test-base-factory.patch
    A diff against Temporal's tests/testcore/test_cluster.go, so it carries
    upstream code by construction: its context lines are that file as Temporal
    wrote it.

Not derived: cold/memcold/memcold.go and cold/memcold/factory.go call
Temporal's exported constructors and implement its exported interfaces, and
copy no upstream body; cold/memcold/watermark.go is this repository's own table
and its own SQL; the tests under cold/memcold run Temporal's exported suites
rather than reproducing them.
